# Getting Started with the Cloider Provider

This guide creates a Kubernetes cluster, a PostgreSQL database only the cluster can reach, and a bucket
with an access key for it. It fits in a free Cloider account. The whole configuration is in
[`examples/getting-started`](https://github.com/cloider/terraform-provider-cloider/tree/main/examples/getting-started).

## Before You Begin

* A [Cloider](https://cloider.com) account.
* [Terraform](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/install) 1.5 or later, or
  [OpenTofu](https://opentofu.org/docs/intro/install/) 1.6 or later.
* An API token from the dashboard's **Access Control**, **API Tokens**, with **Read & Write**
  permission. On your own machine, logging in with the [Cloider CLI](https://cloider.com/cli) works too.

## Authenticate

Hand the provider the token in an environment variable:

```shell
export CLOIDER_TOKEN="cldr_..."
```

Or log in with the CLI, whose token the provider uses when no other is set:

```shell
cloider login
```

